# Turkish text and encoding

All user-facing copy, error messages, seed data, and test names are Turkish. Files are UTF-8 without BOM.

## Shell (Windows PowerShell 5.1)

PowerShell 5.1 reads BOM-less UTF-8 as ANSI, so `Get-Content` shows `boş` as `bo�Y`. That is a display artifact, not file corruption.

- Read and edit files with the Read and StrReplace/Write tools, not shell commands.
- If a shell read is unavoidable, pass `-Encoding UTF8`.
- Never write source files with `Set-Content`, `Out-File`, or `>`; they re-encode and corrupt Turkish characters.

## Locale-aware string handling

Default casing breaks Turkish `I/ı` and `İ/i`:

```ts
// ❌ "İzin".toLowerCase() === "i̇zin" (dotted i + combining mark)
row.subject.toLowerCase().includes(query.toLowerCase());

// ✅ back-end/src/shared/http.ts
includesTr(row.subject, query);
// or value.toLocaleLowerCase("tr-TR")
```

- Format dates for display with the `tr-TR` locale.
- Use the exact Turkish domain terms from `PROJE_TANIMI.md` (statuses, priorities, section names); do not translate or paraphrase them in code, UI, or API messages.
- Identifiers, types, and code comments stay in English.
